CASE_DESCRIPTION:
Emission Registration System (ERS) contains an incorrect test value. This concerns the 24-hour average emission limit value for the continuously measured emission component CxHy at installation HRSG: it should be max. 2.2 mg/nm3 (15% O2), but appears to be incorrectly set at 3.0 mg/nm3. The test when each 24-hour average occurs therefore wrongly does not signal that an operating report must be made if there is a peak between 2.2 and 3.0 mg/nm3.
HIrefore, operating notifications to DCMR have failed to occur for the exceedances of the 24-hour average emission limit value for CxHy at HRSG:
- 2.22 mg/nm3 dd 31 July;
- 2.23 mg/nm3 dd 11 August;
- 2.31 mg/nm3 dd 14 August.
Notification to DCMR about all this by email is enclosed.

7. rubbish
@Wallbaum, Peter please have the area in 40UVC and 40UVF cleaned.
There is a lot of rubbish in the outdoor area and in the buildings. A report will be posted.

